# Maintained HTML tokenizer subset specification, version 2.
# Authored for W; no translated/generated third-party grammar material.
# Offsets count bytes of the original explicit-length input.

space       := U+0009 | U+000A | U+000C | U+000D | U+0020
alpha       := ASCII A-Z | ASCII a-z
name        := alpha (any-byte - space - '/' - '>')*
attribute-name := (any-byte - space - '=' - '/' - '>')+
attribute   := attribute-name (space* '=' space* value)?
value       := '"' any-byte-except-double-quote* '"'
             | "'" any-byte-except-single-quote* "'"
             | (any-byte - space - '>')*
start-tag   := '<' name (space* attribute)* space* '/'? '>'
end-tag     := '</' name (space* attribute)* space* '/'? '>'
comment     := '<!--' bytes-until-first('-->') '-->'
doctype     := case-insensitive('<!doctype') (space | '>') ... '>'
bogus       := ('<!' | '<?') bytes-until-first('>') '>'
reference   := '&' ('amp' | 'lt' | 'gt' | 'quot' | 'apos' | 'nbsp') ';'
             | '&#' decimal-digits ';' | '&#' ('x' | 'X') hex-digits ';'

State DATA: '<' followed by alpha starts a tag; '</' followed by alpha starts
an end tag. '<!--' starts COMMENT. '<!'/'<?' start DOCTYPE/BOGUS. Other '<'
bytes are ordinary text. Text ends before the next '<' (invalid '<' starts a
new text token). Decode references in text and attribute values.

State RCDATA: entered by title/textarea starts. Text, including '<', continues
until a case-insensitive matching '</name' followed by space, '/', or '>'.
Decode references. Matching close is processed as END_TAG and returns to DATA.

State RAWTEXT: entered by style/xmp/iframe/noembed/noframes.
Same close recognition as RCDATA, with reference decoding disabled.

State SCRIPT: entered by script. References remain literal. Normal and escaped
text recognize the same matching close as RAWTEXT. '<!--' in normal text enters
escaped text (with two trailing dashes). In escaped text, case-insensitive
'<script' followed by space, '/', or '>' enters double-escaped text. There,
case-insensitive '</script' with the same delimiter returns to escaped text,
retaining the entire spelling as text. '-->' in either escape mode returns to
normal script data. EOF in an escape mode emits a diagnostic. JS quoting and
comments do not hide HTML delimiters. Each script text run is one token.

Tag names and attribute names are ASCII lowercase. First duplicate attribute
wins. Slash before '>' sets self_closing; stray slash diagnoses and advances.
EOF in a quoted value, tag, comment, or declaration emits its partial token and
a diagnostic. Unterminated raw text emits text through EOF. Every call advances
or returns EOF. Resource failures return EOF and set tokenizer.failed.

In decoded text, CRLF/CR become LF, NUL becomes U+FFFD, and invalid numeric
Unicode scalar values become U+FFFD. Unknown references remain literal.
This lexical specification accompanies html.w and tests/html_test.w; tree
recovery and excluded standard algorithms are in docs/projects/html.md.
